@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g6-nouns`
IMPORT `g6-schedule-three`
IMPORT `g6-amount`
IMPORT `int-commencement`
IMPORT `int-work`

-- int-sanction.l4: integration points IP9, IP12 and IP16, and headline (c): what is the sanction for this violation.
-- The INTEGRATOR's module.  The violation comes from a producer (groups 1, 3 or 5, through int-work); Chapter 6 must have been in
-- force on the day of the act (group 7, s.63(b)); the amount is group 6's: the Third Schedule's column B, updated by the index on the
-- day s.47(a) fixes, plus the s.45(a) addition for a continuing violation and the s.45(b) addition for a repeat violation.
--
-- What is NOT defaulted here.
--   * Chapter 6 in force: group 7 refuses while no regulation under s.46 is known and the first limb of s.63(b) has run.  The refusal
--     is returned, not turned into FALSE.  A caller who wants to price a violation on a stated hypothesis passes the facts that
--     fix the commencement with a hypothetical s.46 date (int-commencement).
--   * The index readings, the first update year and the day s.47(a) fixes are inputs: the sources give none of them.
--   * A dash in the corporation column (items (1), (2) and (4)) is group 6's named refusal; it stays one.
-- What the answer means.  The facts breach nothing the Third Schedule prices; or Chapter 6 had not commenced on the day of the act,
-- so no sanction is payable; or a sanction of a stated amount.  Group 6 does not ask here whether the Commissioner holds the
-- Minister's authorisation (s.41(a)): that is a precondition of imposing, not part of the amount.

§ `Integration points IP9, IP12, IP16 and headline (c): the sanction`

@ref Law s.41, s.45, s.47, s.63(b)
@desc What the Law says about the sanction for the facts of a case: nothing is priced, or Chapter 6 had not commenced, or a sanction of an amount
DECLARE `Answer on the sanction for a violation` IS ONE OF
    `no listed violation: the facts breach no provision that the Third Schedule prices`
    `no sanction: Chapter 6 had not commenced on the day of the act`
    `the sanction is` HAS `the amount in new shekels` IS A NUMBER

@ref Law s.45, s.47
@desc The facts a sanction is priced from beyond the violation itself: how long a continuing violation continued, the violator's earlier violations, the day s.47(a) fixes for the update, the year of the first update day and the readings of the index
DECLARE `Facts for pricing a violation` HAS
    `the violation continued from` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The day a continuing violation started; NOTHING if it is not a continuing violation (s.45(a))
    `the last day the violation continued` IS A DATE @desc The last day the violation continued; read only for a continuing violation
    `the previous violations of the violator` IS A LIST OF `Previous violation` @desc The violator's earlier violations, each with its item, its day and whether a sanction was imposed or a conviction obtained (s.45(b))
    `the day on which the amount is updated` IS A DATE @desc The day s.47(a) fixes for the update: the day the payment demand was delivered, or the notice of intention for a violator who made no representations, or the day of the decision on a stayed appeal
    `the year of the first update day` IS A NUMBER @desc The year of the first 1 January on which the amounts are updated; the sources do not say which (group 6, fork F-FIRST)
    `the index readings` IS A LIST OF `Price index reading` @desc The consumer price index readings with their months and days of publication; the sources contain none

@ref Law s.45(a)
@desc The number of whole months a continuing violation continued, as group 6 counts them (0 if it is not a continuing violation)
GIVEN pricing IS A `Facts for pricing a violation`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`int — the months of continuation in` pricing MEANS
    CONSIDER pricing's `the violation continued from`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0
    WHEN JUST start THEN `s 45(a) — the whole months a violation continued from` start `to` (pricing's `the last day the violation continued`)

@ref Law s.41, s.45, s.46, s.47, s.63(b) (IP9, IP12, IP16)
@export What the Law says the sanction is for a violation, if there is one: nothing if the facts breach no provision the Third Schedule prices; no sanction if Chapter 6 had not commenced on the day of the act; otherwise the amount, the Third Schedule's column B updated by the index plus the additions for a continuing and for a repeat violation; a named refusal where the Law gives no amount (a dash in the corporation column) or where a group's answer is a refusal (Chapter 6 with no regulation under s.46 known, an index that cannot be read)
GIVEN violation IS A MAYBE Violation @desc The violation a producer found, if any
      pricing IS A `Facts for pricing a violation` @desc How long it continued, the earlier violations and the indexation inputs
      facts IS A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63` @desc The Law's publication day, the day the section 59 regulations came into force and the day any section 46 regulations came into force
GIVETH AN `Answer on the sanction for a violation`
`int — the sanction for` violation `priced from` pricing `with the commencement` facts MEANS
    CONSIDER violation
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `no listed violation: the facts breach no provision that the Third Schedule prices`
    WHEN JUST v THEN
        IF   `int — Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act, given the facts` (v's `date of the act`) facts
        THEN `the sanction is`
                 (`s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation`
                      v
                      (`int — the months of continuation in` pricing)
                      (`s 45(b) — the violation` v `is a repeat violation, given` (pricing's `the previous violations of the violator`))
                      (pricing's `the day on which the amount is updated`)
                      (pricing's `the year of the first update day`)
                      (pricing's `the index readings`))
        ELSE `no sanction: Chapter 6 had not commenced on the day of the act`

@ref Law s.3(a), Third Schedule items (1), (2); s.41 and following
@export The sanction for the work of a situation: group 1's violation under s.3(a), if any, priced by group 6
GIVEN s IS A `Situation of one piece of work` @desc The person, their licences, the day, the system and the act
      reference IS A STRING @desc A reference that identifies the act
      pricing IS A `Facts for pricing a violation` @desc How long it continued, the earlier violations and the indexation inputs
      facts IS A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63` @desc The facts that fix the commencement
GIVETH AN `Answer on the sanction for a violation`
`int — the sanction for the work of` s `with the reference` reference `priced from` pricing `with the commencement` facts MEANS
    `int — the sanction for` (`int — the violation committed under section 3(a) by` s `with the reference` reference) `priced from` pricing `with the commencement` facts

@ref Law s.18(a), Third Schedule items (5) and (6); s.41 and following
@export The sanction for an engagement: group 3's violation under s.18(a), if any, priced by group 6
GIVEN e IS A `Situation of one engagement` @desc The operator, the engaged person, the day and the system
      reference IS A STRING @desc A reference that identifies the act
      pricing IS A `Facts for pricing a violation` @desc How long it continued, the earlier violations and the indexation inputs
      facts IS A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63` @desc The facts that fix the commencement
GIVETH AN `Answer on the sanction for a violation`
`int — the sanction for the engagement` e `with the reference` reference `priced from` pricing `with the commencement` facts MEANS
    `int — the sanction for` (`int — the violation committed under section 18(a) in` e `with the reference` reference) `priced from` pricing `with the commencement` facts

@ref Law s.4, Third Schedule item (3); s.41 and following
@export The sanction for a self-description: group 1's violation under s.4, if any, priced by group 6
GIVEN s IS A `Situation of one self-description` @desc The person, their licences and the advertisement
      reference IS A STRING @desc A reference that identifies the act
      pricing IS A `Facts for pricing a violation` @desc How long it continued, the earlier violations and the indexation inputs
      facts IS A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63` @desc The facts that fix the commencement
GIVETH AN `Answer on the sanction for a violation`
`int — the sanction for the self-description` s `with the reference` reference `priced from` pricing `with the commencement` facts MEANS
    `int — the sanction for` (`int — the violation committed under section 4 by` s `with the reference` reference) `priced from` pricing `with the commencement` facts
